Design a complete, production-ready STUDENT PORTAL for a college club platform called “SPECTRUM — CLUB AUDITIONS ’26”.

IMPORTANT:
Use the uploaded reference image as the primary visual and art-direction reference.

Recreate the same visual personality, composition language, typography style, photography treatment, handwritten annotations, scrapbook elements, and youthful college atmosphere.

However, this is NOT a landing page.

This is an authenticated STUDENT PORTAL/DASHBOARD used after a student has registered.

The portal must feel like the student has entered the actual Spectrum student ecosystem.

==================================================
1. CORE VISUAL STYLE
==================================================

Create a premium creative-campus interface combining:

- Modern student dashboard
- Editorial magazine design
- Scrapbook aesthetic
- College noticeboard
- Handwritten annotations
- Real campus photography
- Paper textures
- Tape elements
- Doodles
- Small stickers
- Polaroid-inspired image blocks
- Clean modern UI components

The design should feel:

Creative
Young
Energetic
Human
Academic
Social
Premium
Experimental

But NOT messy.

The interface must have strong structure underneath the creative visual layer.

Use the reference image's visual balance:

approximately:
70% clean UI
20% photography / editorial elements
10% decorative scrapbook elements

Do not turn every component into a sticker.

==================================================
2. COLOR PALETTE
==================================================

Use a warm light base.

Primary background:
Warm off-white / paper white

Secondary:
Very light lavender / soft cream

Typography:
Deep charcoal / near-black

Accent colors:
Muted purple
Soft yellow
Coral
Light cyan
Soft pink
Muted green

IMPORTANT:

Use colors selectively.

Do not create rainbow-colored sections.

Each page should have one dominant accent with 1–2 supporting colors.

Avoid:
Neon gradients
Dark cyberpunk UI
Excessive glassmorphism
Heavy shadows
Overly glossy UI

The reference image should feel colorful because of photography, stickers and editorial elements — NOT because every UI component is brightly colored.

==================================================
3. TYPOGRAPHY
==================================================

Use a combination of:

A bold modern sans-serif for navigation and interface.

A heavy handwritten / marker-style display font for selected headings.

A clean sans-serif for body text.

Occasional handwritten annotations should appear around major sections.

Examples:

“YOUR CLUBS”
“WHAT’S NEXT?”
“FIND YOUR TRIBE”
“GOOD PEOPLE. GREAT CLUBS.”
“DON’T MISS THIS.”
“SEE YOU THERE.”

Do not use handwritten fonts for long paragraphs.

